  "comment": "One entry per sound cue. A cue has either file (under public/audio/) or layers: [{file, volume, cents}] that play together (layer volume multiplies the cue's, cents shifts that layer's pitch). volume 0-1. minGapMs: shortest gap between two plays at 1x, multiplied by the playback speed so fast playback plays fewer sounds. rises: pitch climbs by tickPitch.stepCents per step the caller passes. scale: name of an entry in scales (semitone steps, repeating an octave up); the step argument picks the note (1 = first), capped at maxStep (index of the top note); randomStep picks a random note 0..maxStep instead. baseCents: fixed pitch shift (negative is lower). fastFallback: {cue, atSpeed}: at that playback speed or faster, play the named shorter cue instead. limiter: DynamicsCompressorNode values (dB, dB, ratio, s, s) on the final output.",
